PouchDB acts as a local database that mirrors a remote CouchDB instance. When you save a survey, you save it to the local database. When the internet returns, PouchDB syncs the delta automatically.

#### Setting up the Database Service (`db.js`)
```javascript
import PouchDB from 'pouchdb';

// Local database
export const localDB = new PouchDB('field_surveys');

// Remote database (e.g., Cloudant or your own CouchDB instance)
const remoteDB = new PouchDB('https://your-server.com/db/surveys');

// Setup Auto-Sync
export const syncDatabase = () => {
  localDB.sync(remoteDB, {
    live: true,
    retry: true
  }).on('change', (info) => {
    console.log('Syncing data...');
  }).on('error', (err) => {
    console.error('Sync error', err);
  });
};
```

