### 2. Saving Survey Data
Because it is offline-first, you always write to the local database first.

```javascript
const saveSurvey = async (formData) => {
  const doc = {
    _id: new Date().toISOString(), // Unique ID
    ...formData,
    synced: false // Flag for local UI state
  };

  try {
    await localDB.put(doc);
    alert("Saved locally!");
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("Failed to save", err);
  }
};
```

