### 4. Advanced: Handling Conflict Resolution
In field surveying, two people might edit the same record. CouchDB handles this via **Revision IDs (`_rev`)**. If a conflict occurs, you can fetch the document and merge it:

```javascript
localDB.get(id, { conflicts: true }).then((doc) => {
  if (doc._conflicts) {
    // Custom logic: keep your version or merge?
    // Delete the conflicting revision
    localDB.remove(doc._id, doc._conflicts[0]); 
  }
});
```

