### 1. The Single-File Implementation (`index.html`)

You can save this code as an `.html` file and open it in any browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Real-Time Dashboard</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="bg-gray-100 p-8">

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8">Data Dashboard</h1>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
            <!-- Form Section -->
            <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow">
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Add Data Point</h2>
                <form id="dataForm" class="space-y-4">
                    <input type="text" id="label" placeholder="Category (e.g., Q1)" required class="w-full p-2 border rounded">
                    <input type="number" id="value" placeholder="Value" required class="w-full p-2 border rounded">
                    <button type="submit" class="w-full bg-blue-600 text-white p-2 rounded hover:bg-blue-700">Update Chart</button>
                </form>
            </div>

            <!-- Chart Section -->
            <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow">
                <canvas id="myChart"></canvas>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        // Initialize Chart
        const ctx = document.getElementById('myChart').getContext('2d');
        const myChart = new Chart(ctx, {
            type: 'bar',
            data: {
                labels: ['Jan', 'Feb'],
                datasets: [{
                    label: 'Sales Data',
                    data: [12, 19],
                    backgroundColor: 'rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.5)'
                }]
            }
        });

        // Form Handling
        document.getElementById('dataForm').addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
            e.preventDefault();

            const label = document.getElementById('label').value;
            const value = document.getElementById('value').value;

            // Update Chart Data
            myChart.data.labels.push(label);
            myChart.data.datasets[0].data.push(value);

            // Re-render
            myChart.update();

            // Reset Form
            this.reset();
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### 2. Key Components Explained

1.  **Tailwind CSS:** Used via CDN for rapid UI layout. The grid structure (`grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2`) ensures the dashboard is mobile-responsive.
2.  **Chart.js:** A robust library for canvas-based rendering. We initialize it with an object containing the chart type, labels, and datasets.
3.  **Event Listener:** The script listens for the `submit` event on the form. It prevents the default browser reload (`e.preventDefault()`), grabs the input values, pushes them into the Chart.js data arrays, and calls `chart.update()`.

