To turn this into a truly "live" dashboard (e.g., updating based on a server feed), replace the form logic with a `setInterval` function:

```javascript
// This will simulate incoming data every 3 seconds
setInterval(() => {
    const randomValue = Math.floor(Math.random() * 20);
    const time = new Date().toLocaleTimeString().slice(-8);

    myChart.data.labels.push(time);
    myChart.data.datasets[0].data.push(randomValue);

    // Keep only the last 10 points for a "rolling" effect
    if(myChart.data.labels.length > 10) {
        myChart.data.labels.shift();
        myChart.data.datasets[0].data.shift();
    }

    myChart.update();
}, 3000);
