#### B. The SPSC Ring Buffer (The Lock-Free Queue)
Using a pre-allocated array of `OrderEvent` objects allows the system to pass events without triggering the Garbage Collector.

```java
public class RingBuffer<T> {
    private final T[] buffer;
    private final int mask;
    private volatile long head = 0;
    private volatile long tail = 0;

    public RingBuffer(int size) {
        this.buffer = (T[]) new Object[size];
        this.mask = size - 1;
    }

    public boolean tryPublish(T event) {
        long currentTail = tail;
        if (currentTail - head >= buffer.length) return false; // Buffer Full
        buffer[(int) (currentTail & mask)] = event;
        tail++;
        return true;
    }
}
```

#### C. The Sequencer (Execution Engine)
The Sequencer is the heartbeat. It runs in a busy-wait loop to minimize latency (never put the thread to sleep).

