### 2. Implementation: The Low-Latency Ring Buffer
The core of high-frequency routing is the **RingBuffer**. Using a power-of-two size allows us to use bitwise masking instead of the expensive modulo operator.

```java
public class MessageRingBuffer {
    private final Message[] buffer;
    private final int mask;
    private final AtomicLong producerCursor = new AtomicLong(-1);

    public MessageRingBuffer(int bufferSize) {
        int size = Integer.highestOneBit(bufferSize - 1) << 1;
        this.buffer = new Message[size];
        this.mask = size - 1;
    }

    public void publish(Message msg) {
        long seq = producerCursor.incrementAndGet();
        buffer[(int) (seq & mask)] = msg;
    }
}
```

