### The Core Design Pattern: `io.CopyBuffer`
Using `io.CopyBuffer` allows us to define an explicit memory limit for the read/write operation. By setting the buffer size to, for example, 32KB, we guarantee the application will not exceed a few megabytes of RAM even when rotating multi-gigabyte files.

