If your daemon needs to monitor many files or network sockets simultaneously, do not use `sleep()` or blocking calls. Use the `epoll` Linux API. It allows the kernel to notify your process *only* when an event happens (Edge-Triggered I/O), resulting in near-zero CPU usage when idle.

