#### B. Hugepages
Allocate the UMEM (the shared memory region for packets) using **Hugepages (2MB or 1GB)**. This significantly reduces TLB misses when the analyzer is iterating over large traffic volumes.

#### C. NUMA Locality
Ensure the NIC and the CPU core running the analyzer are on the same NUMA node. Crossing the QPI/UPI interconnect between CPU sockets will add significant latency and jitter. Use `lscpu` to verify topology.

#### D. Batch Processing
Never process one packet at a time. The function call overhead is too high. Accumulate packets in a buffer and use SIMD instructions (AVX-512) to parse multiple IPv4 headers simultaneously.

