Any high-level language (Python/Go) will introduce GC jitter or overhead that causes packet loss at >1Gbps. By using AF_XDP, you are interacting with the NIC driver at the lowest possible level allowed by the Linux kernel, effectively turning your application into a high-performance network middlebox.

