#### 4. Data Buffering
If you are processing high-speed data (e.g., an accelerometer), do not process data inside the interrupt or main loop. Instead, store data in a **Ring Buffer** and process it in batches to avoid losing data points.

#### 5. Modularity
Keep your hardware abstraction layer (HAL) separate from your business logic. Put your sensor driver code in a separate `.c`/`.h` file from your main application logic. This makes it easier to swap a sensor or switch to a different microcontroller architecture later.

