```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body style="margin:0; overflow:hidden;">
  <script type="module">
    import * as THREE from 'https://cdn.skypack.dev/three@0.132.2';

    // 1. Setup Scene
    const scene = new THREE.Scene();
    const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(75, window.innerWidth/window.innerHeight, 0.1, 1000);
    const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });
    renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
    document.body.appendChild(renderer.domElement);

    // 2. Add Object with Standard Material (supports lighting)
    const geometry = new THREE.TorusKnotGeometry(1, 0.3, 100, 16);
    const material = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0xff4422, roughness: 0.2 });
    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);
    scene.add(mesh);

    // 3. Add Dynamic Lighting
    const light = new THREE.PointLight(0xffffff, 1, 100);
    scene.add(light);
    scene.add(new THREE.AmbientLight(0x404040)); // Soft white light

    camera.position.z = 5;

    // 4. Animation Loop
    function animate(t) {
      requestAnimationFrame(animate);

      // Move light in a circle
      light.position.set(Math.sin(t/500)*3, Math.cos(t/500)*3, 2);

      mesh.rotation.x += 0.01;
      mesh.rotation.y += 0.01;

      renderer.render(scene, camera);
    }
    animate(0);
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Key Components Explained:
1.  **`THREE.Scene`**: The container for all objects, lights, and cameras.
2.  **`MeshStandardMaterial`**: This is a physically-based shader. It automatically calculates how light interacts with the surface (reflections, shadows, and glossiness) without you needing to write raw GLSL code.
3.  **`PointLight`**: A light source that emits in all directions from a specific point. We update its `position` inside the `animate` function to create the "dynamic" lighting effect.
4.  **`requestAnimationFrame`**: A browser API that syncs your code with the monitor's refresh rate, ensuring smooth 60+ FPS performance.

