#### B. The Physics Solver (`PhysicsSystem.cpp`)
This is where the actual math happens. We use **Verlet Integration**: `newPos = pos + (pos - oldPos) + accel * dt * dt`.

```cpp
void UpdatePhysics(std::vector<PhysicsComponent>& entities, float dt) {
    const float damping = 0.99f; // Air resistance

    for (auto& p : entities) {
        if (p.isStatic) continue;

        // 1. Calculate Velocity (implicit)
        Vec3 velocity = (p.position - p.previousPosition) * damping;

        // 2. Verlet Integration
        Vec3 nextPosition = p.position + velocity + (p.acceleration * dt * dt);

        // 3. Update state
        p.previousPosition = p.position;
        p.position = nextPosition;

        // 4. Reset Acceleration (Gravity applied elsewhere)
        p.acceleration = Vec3(0, -9.81f, 0); 
    }
}
```

